Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:03.510
October 18, 2356

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.530
62 Days Until the Great Mission Launch

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:20.100
Don't you think of flying smoothly.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.130
All you've got to think about is to avoid the obstacles and follow me!

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.180
It's easy for you to say.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:29.380
Oops!

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.230
Whoa!

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.150
It's not just the obstacles in front of you.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.480
You must set your eyes way beyond that.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.160
You can't control the Ora-avis with just your reflexes.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.160
The obstacle ahead.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.530
Calculate the relative speed and coordinates.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:05.100
The appropriate evasive route is...

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.790
Enter this data into the guidance equation...

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.080
...and start the next evasive maneuver.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.080
Watch out for the gravity pull...

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.010
Katase...

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:20.710
...Shima?

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.450
It's you again?

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.150
Correct the y-coordinate, z-coordinate 5 degrees.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.030
The tail is being blown!?

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.730
I must activate the counter weight.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.330
Quickly, quickly, I need to put it back up.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:38.240
Go back to the original route and...!

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.290
Argh! Geez! Calm down, Shima!!

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.380
Shipon!? I'll come help you now!

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.000
Taaaahh!

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.810
Brrrrrr! Whoa!

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.180
Arisa...

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.970
...let's leave it to Ms. Leila.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:50.630
Roger that!

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.850
Katase, you tweaked the program again!?

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:03.590
Are you gonna run into everything until the battery is gone!?

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:04.360
Katase!

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:07.610
No! I'm going to stop it on my own!

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.440
I've got to stop it!

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.210
I've got to stop it!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.100
I've got to stop it!

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.540
Argh! Geez!

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.710
Stop!!

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.100
Whoa!

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:32.710
Ouch...

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:46.590
Do you understand  what you have done, Katase?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.720
We couldn't finish even half of the exercise...

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.380
...we were planning to do today.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.010
Because of you, everyone's curriculum is delayed, you know that?

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.060
Yes...

00:05:06.190 --> 00:05:08.040
Do you think Shipon will be okay?

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:08.930
What do you mean?

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.540
I mean, this is already her third time.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.400
Maybe she'll get suspended...

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.380
No way!

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.470
Ms. Leila won't do such a thing.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:18.480
How do you know?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.470
Because it will only delay her study even more.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:24.680
Let's see...

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:29.380
Probably she will be "polishing" this time.

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:30.950
"Polishing?"

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.230
Preparatory student Shima Katase!

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:34.880
As a punishment...

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.570
...I order you to clean the lenses inside the communication laser!

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.770
I have to clean it all by myself...?

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.180
I can't waste any time!

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:54.410
All right!

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.100
I'm gonna do it!

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.290
But with this pace, I'll be polishing this forever.

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:14.580
Turbo?

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.250
What? W-Wait...!!

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:24.040
Argh!

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.820
What the heck is she doing!?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.370
Well, since I've got 10 years of cleaning experience...

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:33.910
We shouldn't spoil her.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:35.290
Why!?

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:38.450
I don't think we should help her either.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:40.060
Yayoi!?

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:44.110
If we help her, she'll feel even more guilty.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:45.320
Hmm...

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.120
But as her best friend...

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:51.190
Hey, but you don't want to be seen by your best friend...

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.240
Whoa! W-Wait! Shipon! ...when you are doing

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.560
the punishment, do you?

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:58.070
Hang in there...

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:03.390
Hey, I heard...

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.770
You were body slammed by Shima Katase?

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:06.630
Yeah.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.700
Thanks to her, even my Bianca's been put out of service.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:13.950
I think she's got great skill, shooting down the famous Leila Barthes.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:15.310
That was unexpected!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:19.760
Besides, what she should be learning is not to body slam, but to avoid!

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:21.000
Well, that's true.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.420
Besides...

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.890
Even if she has quite a programming skill, her flying skill is...

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:29.740
Maybe she should focus on desk work from now on.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:31.990
It's too late already when something serious happens.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:33.740
Now, now...

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.730
Her training has just started.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.380
Let's give her more time and see what happens.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.880
But...

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.280
It's up to her after all.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.350
Whether she wants to proceed or go back.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:52.610
She's got such unbalanced skills.

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:56.030
Her programming skill is excellent, but her flying skill is awful...

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.730
But that clumsiness makes her sort of cute.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.370
Hey, now...

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:01.860
Humph!

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:05.560
Well, if she could have done it without instructions...

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:07.710
...there is no need for us instructors.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:11.380
The worthiness of instructors...

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:14.440
...will be measured by the number of students with difficulties.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.100
It's very ironic.

00:08:25.490 --> 00:08:29.480
Foundations are built on the orbits of the solar system's planets...

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:34.130
...and they will create these giant barriers to protect each planet.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:39.340
This will be the umbrella to protect the Earth from the Second Wave.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.610
I know about the Great Mission already.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.820
So what kind of information did you get this time?

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.290
Hmm? Right...

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.880
Well, while each Foundation is blocking the Second Wave...

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:56.600
...the Ora-avis Machines must provide support.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:59.930
To keep the strength of the barriers even, right?

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.050
That's right.

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:05.220
And some of the students may be chosen to be the pilots?

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.570
Well, they might be considering that option, that's all.

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.600
To witness the Second Wave firsthand...

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.800
It's like being a witness to history itself.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.530
Ayaka will be so excited when she hears about this.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:23.810
Speaking of which, where is Ayaka?

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:25.680
She's working on her Katie.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:27.110
She's a hard worker, isn't she?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.850
She's a hard worker, yet still a genius...

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.370
I can't compete with her...

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:39.920
Hmm?

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:51.240
Ouch...

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.140
Oh...

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.700
Are you... all right?

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.020
Y-You are one of the Big 4...

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:06.180
Punishment? That's too bad.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:09.860
Um, yes, you are right.

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:12.630
I've been polishing and polishing, but there's no end to it...

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.750
And now I don't remember how far I polished.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:19.910
And I thought I was finally done, then it goes "Boom!"

00:10:23.530 --> 00:10:25.980
I'm not so lucky since I got here.

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:36.990
U-Um...

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:41.020
I've never been punished since being admitted to this school.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.210
Oh...

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.690
I guess I've been very lucky then.

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:50.710
No... I don't think so...

00:10:51.570 --> 00:10:52.150
That's right.

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.960
What you are lacking is not luck.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:56.300
It's your skills!

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.020
Where do you think Shipon went?

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:27.490
The storage room is right by the Katie hangar, so...

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.070
You know your way around.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.410
Yayoi, when did you receive the punishment?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.540
I've heard from someone.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.470
That's one of the Big 4...

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:45.070
Ms. Ayaka Machida.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.100
Geez!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:56.970
She's kind of hard to approach...

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.970
No wonder she is one of the Big 4.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:01.740
Ms. Machida.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:06.410
Um...

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:09.750
Have you seen my friend?

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:11.880
Your friend?

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.020
Ah.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.080
I saw her, but I don't think you can find her.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.690
What do you mean?

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:24.340
That girl...

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.290
She may be leaving the Stellvia.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:38.710
Now this is...

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.990
Where am I?

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.210
Ms. Katase!

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:46.660
Hi!

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:49.520
Is it... Otoyama?

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:59.040
Do you always carry the compeito around with you?

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:01.100
Yeah. Always a handful.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.670
It's like... a lucky charm.

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:05.490
Hmm...

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.100
What were you doing here, by the way, Otoyama?

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.600
How about you?

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:14.970
I think this is the restricted area.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.320
Y-Yeah...

00:13:16.710 --> 00:13:19.340
I was looking for a place where nobody can find me.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:20.580
Hmm...

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:21.950
Oh, that's right!

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.440
You were kind of depressed, huh?

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:25.320
Because of that class earlier.

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.090
I tried to stop, you know.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:31.020
But while I was thinking about calculating the new flying route...

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.500
...or regulating the balance...

00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:36.570
Next thing I knew, I was body slamming Ms. Leila.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:38.220
Hmm...

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:40.700
I'm no good...

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:44.370
It's like so much information starts attacking me at once...

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:46.380
...as soon as I get into the plane.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:47.750
Then you shouldn't watch them.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:48.400
What?

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:51.520
Data is just a clue.

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.100
You can ignore some, you know.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:56.120
You can't do things like that.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:57.600
Hmm...

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.030
I think that a gap between each piece of information...

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.140
...is filled automatically by our own brain.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:08.730
You put a little bit of salt in a sweet snack, right?

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:10.440
I think it's something like that.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:12.690
Huh?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.670
Salt will bring out the sweetness...

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:16.330
Right, a hidden spice!

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:17.980
I see...

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.690
Welcome home, Shipon!

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.210
I stayed here to wait for you to come back.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:33.100
Arisa went out looking for you, Shipon.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:34.320
Is that so...

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.160
You left a mop out, you know.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:38.050
What?

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:40.130
Oh, sorry...

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.660
Come on, cheer up.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.380
Nobody can be an expert from the beginning.

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:48.030
But you're so good at flying from beginning...

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:48.710
What?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.710
I'm no good...

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:53.540
I can't fly it like you do.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.450
Actually...

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.080
I'm cheating a little bit.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:02.830
What?

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.280
This is my second try.. as a preparatory student.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.610
Two years ago.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:15.440
I've already joined this academy once.

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:18.880
I was here for 6 months, but I dropped out.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:20.700
How come?

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:24.260
An accident.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:25.680
That's why I dropped out.

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:30.590
I guess I was too careless because my grades were so good.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:37.130
I lost control of Bianca, and I was thrown outside the training area.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:40.800
Ms. Leila came to rescue me finally.

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:45.190
But until then, I was all by myself inside Bianca.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:49.300
That's when I thought space can be very frightening.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:54.560
Space is a scary place, Shipon.

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:57.170
Once you're out there, you're truly alone.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:15:59.830
There is nothing you can rely on...

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:03.010
So you must train yourself.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:11.720
I think Ms. Leila knows that being too nice to us won't do any good after all.

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:16.800
I realized that when I was lying in the bed at the hospital.

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:21.270
That's why I think I was able to come back to the Stellvia.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.070
I want to go back to space...

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.170
How about you, Shipon?

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.980
Me? I'm...

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:01.300
I'm...

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:05.810
I'm home...

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:08.180
Oh! Arisa!

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:09.780
Shipon!!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:10.990
Arisa!

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:14.950
Stop it!

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:17.180
Hey, hey, how about it!?

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:19.900
You made us so worried!!

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:20.590
I'm sorry!

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:23.220
You are gonna pay for this!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.960
Ouch!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.960
Ouch!

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:27.440
Come on! I'm gonna tickle you to death!

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:27.040
No! Please stop! Stop it!!

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.110
Humph, so stupid...

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:34.270
Did Shipon come home?

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:36.970
Kouta told us that she must be home by now...

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.360
It's kind of naughty...!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:40.010
Huh?

00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:43.230
Hey! Don't come into a girl's room unless you're invited!

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:45.050
What, aren't we friends?

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:48.020
Girls only! You guys, out!

00:17:48.210 --> 00:17:50.400
We want to come in because we are boys!

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:51.260
That's right!

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:52.290
Pervert!

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:53.520
Because we are boys!

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.960
You let us in at the study group!

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:57.520
You are not allowed in here!

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.940
Releasing the air. Opening the gate!

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.650
We are taking the same course as last week.

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.070
Set the navigation equation to B.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.220
Shima Katase...

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:29.090
Her grade from the simulation training on the ground was A.

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:29.870
And...

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.580
...she's got the recommendation from Richard.

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:36.100
What kind of student is she anyway?

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:40.570
Obstacle ahead.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:43.730
Confirm the relative position, speed, and evasive route!

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.960
Minimize the difference between those two routes.

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:49.220
And the distance to the next obstacle is...

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.480
L-Let's see...

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:57.720
M-Must choose the evasive route...!

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:11.250
A hidden spice, hidden spice!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:12.180
Oh...

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.010
"Data is just a clue..."

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:26.290
"You can ignore some..." No problem!

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:30.950
I did it!

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:33.460
Katase...

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:52.810
Shipon! Shipon!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:52.780
Hey!

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.470
Wow! Grade B!

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:56.710
That's a huge improvement!

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:58.280
What did you do!?

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:00.880
Yeah. I think a hidden spice worked...

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:02.060
Huh, what?

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.850
What is that? You are weird.

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:08.510
Katase!

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:12.120
Ms. Leila...

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:21.290
Your control of the plane is still no good!

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:23.460
Think of how to balance the plane!

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:26.000
This is your navigation record.

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:27.770
Look here.

00:20:28.230 --> 00:20:29.110
Katase, take a look.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.150
Y-Yes...

00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.820
The plane's speed and movement are so far apart.

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:37.450
That's why you had a tough time avoiding the next obstacle.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:38.320
Yes...

00:20:38.760 --> 00:20:40.490
Try balancing the plane more.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:44.800
It's your bad habit to forget about keeping the balance...

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:46.070
...while you're thinking of maneuvering position.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:47.930
You'd better correct that soon.

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:48.730
What?

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:52.370
27% of the penalties you suffered at the simulation training...

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:54.770
...on the ground were because of this lack of balance.

00:20:55.820 --> 00:21:00.960
And about your acceleration technique, Bianca has no problem...

00:20:56.410 --> 00:21:00.240
Ms. Leila even took out my old data...?

00:21:00.990 --> 00:21:02.840
...taking that kind of abuse, but the pilot will not be able to take it.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.920
In a case like this... Katase?

00:21:07.040 --> 00:21:07.530
Oh...

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:09.780
Are you listening to me?

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.410
Yes, thank you so much, Ms. Leila.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:18.370
Ayaka.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:20.330
It's final.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:25.340
They've decided to take some of the students for the Great Mission.

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:27.970
Is that right?

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:32.400
But... only 20 will be chosen from all Foundations.

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:34.740
It's gonna be extremely tough...

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:38.790
Even if it's a long shot...

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:44.950
If the door is open, then I will go into that door.

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:48.450
No matter what.

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:55.040
Episode 4:
I'll Do My Best!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

